CORRECTION: retract v1.43 compiler claim — it is v1.44 (ELF e_machine proof)

I was wrong to pin v1.43 for pump/pump_amm/pump_fees. The ELF e_machine header is the
definitive discriminator: originals = 263 (EM_SBF); a v1.43 build = 247 (EM_BPF, old
format); a v1.44 build = 263 (matches). platform-tools v1.43 emits the wrong machine type,
so it cannot be the compiler regardless of .text size (my section-size argument missed the
header). v1.44 is correct — as status.json / build_reconstruction_candidate.py already have.

Adds COMPILER-CORRECTION.md, banners RECIPE-REVERSE-ENGINEERING.md + FULL-GAP-REPORT.md,
and REMOVES the three v1.43-recipe-switch candidates (they carried e_machine=247, header-
incompatible) with a RETRACTED.md. The compiler-independent findings (SDK coverage, the
oracle-verified token-incentive recovery, version boundaries, the lost-source byte-identical
limit) stand.

